{"_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": ""}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "CASE, Computer Aided Software Engineering"}, {"type": "position", "content": 8}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 1}, {"type": "level", "content": "A2.2"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you use to describe CASE."}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Identify key information about people's jobs and places of work in spoken or written contexts.  Make the information system design report, based on the selection of both hardware and software tools required for the IT solution."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Understands important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level.   Exchanges simple information on the design of an information system, computer architecture and hardware, and basic concepts on graphic design."}], "type": "objectives"}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "enpe8n4le01ob08re1img01.jpg"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Comparatives Using as\u2026 as"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You can use <span class=\"strong\">as\u2026as</span> to compare things when the things we are comparing are the same in a certain way."}, {"type": "example", "content": "And, the second ones, the Lower CASE tools, which are as important as the first ones."}, {"type": "text", "content": "To make a comparative statement with \u201c<span class=\"italic\">as </span>\u201d you follow this structure:"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<p style=\"text-align: center;\">S+ Verb + <strong>As</strong> + Adjective + <strong>As </strong>+ Complement</p>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Examples:"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<li><span class=\"italic\">This new software program is <span class=\"strong\">as complex as its </span> previous version. </span> <li><span class=\"italic\">The software tools of this application are <span class=\"strong\">as convenient as </span> the ones of that other application. </span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Notice that when you compare with <span class=\"italic\">as\u2026 as</span>  the adjective remains the same."}, {"type": "text", "content": "On the other hand, you can conclude that two things are different by comparing with <span class=\"italic\">as\u2026as </span> in the negative form."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Structure:"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<p style=\"text-align: center;\">S+ Verb + <strong>Not</strong> + <strong>As</strong> + Adjective + <strong>As </strong>+ Complement</p>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Examples:"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<li><span class=\"italic\">This new software program is <span class=\"strong\">not as  complex as its </span> previous version. </span> <li><span class=\"italic\">The software tools of this application are <span class=\"strong\">not as convenient as </span> the ones of that other application. </span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Notice that in this kind of comparisons, the first named thing has an inferior connotation than the second one."}, {"type": "example", "content": "This one is as essential as CASE in any process that implies creation tools."}, {"type": "example", "content": "It results as useful as CASE to improve the productivity and the quality in any particular task."}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Collocations with Different Verbs Related to Computers"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "A <span class=\"strong\">collocatio</span>n is a word that fits correctly with other word. And, both together make a natural and proper sense."}, {"type": "example", "content": "The Upper CASE tools, specialized in business maintenance, access to data and data transferring, as flow diagrams and decision tables."}, {"type": "text", "content": "<p><span class=\"strong\">Collocations</span> in Technology field are very usual.</p> <p>In the chart below you can check some common verb collocations related to computers:</p>"}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":1,\"columns\":1,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"COMPUTERS COLLOCATIONS\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}"}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":11,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\"><span class=\\\"strong\\\">VERB </span> </div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\"><span class=\\\"strong\\\">WORDS </span> </div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\"><span class=\\\"strong\\\">Access </span> </div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Access information, access data\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\"><span class=\\\"strong\\\">Boot up/ Start up </span> </div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Boot up/ start up the computer\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\"><span class=\\\"strong\\\">Check </span> </div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Check e-mail\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\"><span class=\\\"strong\\\">Delete </span> </div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Delete a file, delete a program, delete a picture\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\"><span class=\\\"strong\\\">Log on/ Log off </span> </div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Log on/ log off (to) the internet, log on/ log off